{{en-noun}}

# A person from the continent of [[Asia]], or a descendant thereof - especially:
## {{lb|en|US|Canada|Australia|NZ|also [[w: International English|International English on the Internet]]}} A person from or with ancestry in East or Southeast Asia, occasionally South Asia.
## {{lb|en|UK|Ireland|South Africa}} A person from or with ancestry in South Asia.
##* {{quote-journal|en|passage=If radio and television programmes are anything to go by, '''Asians''' in Britain get up early on a Sunday.|title=Movie Mahal: Indian cinema on ITV Channel 4|work=Popular Music|year=1987|month=May|author=Paul Oliver|page=215|doi=10.1017/S0261143000002774}}
##* {{quote-text|en|year=2013|author=Malala Yousafzai|title=I Am Malala
|passage=Were there Taliban beheading people? I didn't tell my parents, but I flinched if an '''Asian'''-looking man came close.}}
# A [[domestic cat]] of a [[breed]] similar to the [[Burmese]].

====Usage notes====
The American usage of "''Asian''" (East, Southeast, sometimes South Asian) is internationally used outside of English (e.g. in Turkish, German, Swedish, Korean, French, etc.).

